  "body": "## What changed\n\nUpdate only the count matcher in `crates/app/tests/pocket3d_hsm.rs`.\nThe unmeasured-platform branch calls a pure helper.\nThe helper accepts the current solidcore counts with the existing small band widths:\n\n- Moves: `4673..=4703`.\n- Planar feeds: `4645..=4675`.\n- Arcs: `1970..=1990`.\n\nThree portable tests check the current pin, every boundary, adjacent outside counts, and old mesh readings.\nThe exact platform pins, mesh assertion and safety assertions do not change.\nNo production code, goldens, process files or shared changelog changes.\nThe decision is in `docs/decisions/3085-bore-fallback-band.md`.\n\n## Why these counts\n\nThe issue proposes `(3158, 3130, 1141)`, but that reading is now outdated.\nCommit `2407d9b09` records `(4688, 4660, 1980)` after the solidcore bump in PR #3802.\nThe documented Linux mesh changed from 6228 to 5232 facets.\nWindows measured the same new triple. The existing macOS comment still states its measurement limit.\nThe fallback keeps its previous half-widths: 15 moves, 15 planar feeds and 10 arcs.\nThis uses the issue's unit-test acceptance alternative. It is not a measurement on a fourth platform.\n\n## Checks on head 72eeb3e976be9bdbcc5dcaebbe1ba8e7679e5c77\n\n- `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=3 cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: PASS. The selected `app suites: pocket3d_hsm` step passed.\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo test -p camcraft-app --test pocket3d_hsm`: PASS, 5 passed and 2 ignored.\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test pocket3d_hsm -- -D warnings`: PASS.\n- `git diff origin/main...HEAD --check`: PASS.\n\nNamed regression tests:\n\n- `the_unmeasured_bore_band_accepts_the_current_pin`.\n- `the_unmeasured_bore_band_checks_each_boundary`.\n- `the_unmeasured_bore_band_rejects_the_old_mesh_readings`.\n\nThe unchanged `the_linux_x86_64_bore_count_pin_is_exact` also passed.\nRestoring the old fallback made all three new tests fail. Restoring the fix made the selected suite pass.\n\n## Not exercised and limits\n\nThe heavy bore generation and known-fail #1950 test remain ignored.\nNo fourth-platform, Windows or macOS execution is claimed.\nThe universal light lane was not run. Its broad release build conflicts with this bounded, test-only task scope.\nNo full app/workspace, catalog, GUI or release rebuild was run.\n`rustfmt --check` reports differences on both the unchanged baseline and final file. The existing compact style is retained.\n`graphify` is not installed here; no generated graph was changed.\nGitHub reports no required checks for `main`. No green CI result is claimed.\n\nEffort: low. No escalation.\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #3085\n",
